(2814083, 388807, 48560, '<td valign="top">simply beautiful</td>', 'simply beautiful', '2006-09-08 05:54:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814221, 390399, 38032, '<td valign="top">Aside from the fact that this is a picture of a pretty-much unquestionable sexy pose on an attractive girl, the elements here are just unfathomable - I really can''t get over this and I think you''ll have many faves.  The juxtaposition of the gold bikini and shanti-industrial feeling in the background with the steam --- wow --- The colors can pass for pastel but I think that might be the only thing that keeps it out of the blue -- perhaps a red is in order :)</td>', 'Aside from the fact that this is a picture of a pretty-much unquestionable sexy pose on an attractive girl, the elements here are just unfathomable - I really can''t get over this and I think you''ll have many faves.  The juxtaposition of the gold bikini and shanti-industrial feeling in the background with the steam --- wow --- The colors can pass for pastel but I think that might be the only thing that keeps it out of the blue -- perhaps a red is in order :)', '2006-09-08 08:08:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814241, 390383, 38032, '<td valign="top">Ths has a wow factor and great photographic quality.  The colors are great ... The newpaper in the foreground is perfect ... but something seems to be just a bit forced. WARNING: constructive criticism coming:  I think if the background were a city landscape or maybe the model had a sliightly more natural  in-motion pose it would be more graspable for me. I love the idea and by all means this should be in the top 20 -- I''m just telling you what would make it a 10 for me.  I gave this a 7</td>', 'Ths has a wow factor and great photographic quality.  The colors are great ... The newpaper in the foreground is perfect ... but something seems to be just a bit forced. WARNING: constructive criticism coming:  I think if the background were a city landscape or maybe the model had a sliightly more natural  in-motion pose it would be more graspable for me. I love the idea and by all means this should be in the top 20 -- I''m just telling you what would make it a 10 for me.  I gave this a 7', '2006-09-08 08:16:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814397, 390334, 16004, '<td valign="top">it''s funny, but the title very much invokes such a hippie, time specific feeling.  i know it was the year of punk, but still...   i did think of beach huts as a possible subject, but couldn''t really find any that would fit in sense of colour or be photognic enough.  this does the first and is the second.  i like the contrast between the blue and yellow and yellow and blue groups of huts a lot, though it does have the affect of unbalancing the composition a bit (to me it feels more natural cropping everything left of the space just left of centre).  the skies are effective, as is the lack of people.  really like this image very much. 8.</td>', 'it''s funny, but the title very much invokes such a hippie, time specific feeling.  i know it was the year of punk, but still...   i did think of beach huts as a possible subject, but couldn''t really find any that would fit in sense of colour or be photognic enough.  this does the first and is the second.  i like the contrast between the blue and yellow and yellow and blue groups of huts a lot, though it does have the affect of unbalancing the composition a bit (to me it feels more natural cropping everything left of the space just left of centre).  the skies are effective, as is the lack of people.  really like this image very much. 8.', '2006-09-08 09:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814416, 387126, 16004, '<td valign="top">my goodness, SO cutely adorable!  bunny!  this is a really cute photograph, and it certainly fits the challenge.  there are a few composition issues i have, particularly with the cropping off of the bunny bottom.  it also feels too close, and you''ve seemed to have lost the opportunity of really conveying his tiny size - being in a human hand, or something similar (tea pots are always good) might have been more effective than a similar sized fruit.  his ears and back could also do with being a tad sharper, and i can see you in his eye which is a minor distraction.  still adorably cute though, and because of the cuteness (and great choice of subject) it bashes my criticism and gropes my heart.  7.  aww! bunny!</td>', 'my goodness, SO cutely adorable!  bunny!  this is a really cute photograph, and it certainly fits the challenge.  there are a few composition issues i have, particularly with the cropping off of the bunny bottom.  it also feels too close, and you''ve seemed to have lost the opportunity of really conveying his tiny size - being in a human hand, or something similar (tea pots are always good) might have been more effective than a similar sized fruit.  his ears and back could also do with being a tad sharper, and i can see you in his eye which is a minor distraction.  still adorably cute though, and because of the cuteness (and great choice of subject) it bashes my criticism and gropes my heart.  7.  aww! bunny!', '2006-09-08 09:36:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814443, 390489, 16004, '<td valign="top">okay, as much as i truly love this image, i really don''t get a sense of pastelness in this <i>at all</i>.  okay, the girls skin tone is a bit pale, but really, that''s incidental.  so it doesn''t fit the challenge.<br/> <br/>i wish it did though, ''coz i''d have tenned this no question.  i love the david lynch weirdness about this (though it needs a dwarf!); trying to figure out the narrative here is an intriguing bitch!  there''s a lot to take in here, but it is so rewarding.  i love the building.  the cat looking at the bird and the girl looking at the cat is fantastically entertaining, so heirarchical...  and can i say: strapless dress <i>and</i> top hat?  GENIUS!  technically it''s great; the composition is certainly unconventional but it is successful, the colours are rich (too rich - should be pastelly), the building has a texture you can see...  probably my favourite picture of the year.  it''ll be unfair to give a 10, so 8.  okay, 9.</td>', 'okay, as much as i truly love this image, i really don''t get a sense of pastelness in this at all.  okay, the girls skin tone is a bit pale, but really, that''s incidental.  so it doesn''t fit the challenge. i wish it did though, ''coz i''d have tenned this no question.  i love the david lynch weirdness about this (though it needs a dwarf!); trying to figure out the narrative here is an intriguing bitch!  there''s a lot to take in here, but it is so rewarding.  i love the building.  the cat looking at the bird and the girl looking at the cat is fantastically entertaining, so heirarchical...  and can i say: strapless dress and top hat?  GENIUS!  technically it''s great; the composition is certainly unconventional but it is successful, the colours are rich (too rich - should be pastelly), the building has a texture you can see...  probably my favourite picture of the year.  it''ll be unfair to give a 10, so 8.  okay, 9.', '2006-09-08 09:50:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814452, 388673, 16004, '<td valign="top">already voted on this - gave it 9.  this is so pretty, and by far the best flower picture in terms of colour, composition and style.  only slight criticism is that i would have liked to have the flowers in the middle of the left half to be less blurry (they in some no mans land between sharp and soft), but that aside, it''s really great.  this is the sort of thing you could sell to Ikea.  the blue is so bright and strong, and really complements the pinks and greenybrowns.   very lovely.</td>', 'already voted on this - gave it 9.  this is so pretty, and by far the best flower picture in terms of colour, composition and style.  only slight criticism is that i would have liked to have the flowers in the middle of the left half to be less blurry (they in some no mans land between sharp and soft), but that aside, it''s really great.  this is the sort of thing you could sell to Ikea.  the blue is so bright and strong, and really complements the pinks and greenybrowns.   very lovely.', '2006-09-08 09:55:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814469, 389119, 16004, '<td valign="top">gorgeous cityscape, but unfortunately doesn''t really evoke much sense of "this is a photo about pastels".  the sky is really fantastic, and the illumination of the buildings really dynamic and inviting.  i love the angularness, and the patterns of lines...  the orange lights on the right distract a bit, as does the single light on the extreme left, but i sympathise with wanting to maximise your wide angle because as a whole it looks great.  just wished it fit the challenge more.  8.</td>', 'gorgeous cityscape, but unfortunately doesn''t really evoke much sense of "this is a photo about pastels".  the sky is really fantastic, and the illumination of the buildings really dynamic and inviting.  i love the angularness, and the patterns of lines...  the orange lights on the right distract a bit, as does the single light on the extreme left, but i sympathise with wanting to maximise your wide angle because as a whole it looks great.  just wished it fit the challenge more.  8.', '2006-09-08 09:58:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814475, 389662, 63398, '<td valign="top">Wow!<br/> <br/>I just love this pic!<br/> <br/>What a terrific job of meeting the challenge IMHO.....the softness and beauty of the subjects and the lighting are just awesome.</td>', 'Wow! I just love this pic! What a terrific job of meeting the challenge IMHO.....the softness and beauty of the subjects and the lighting are just awesome.', '2006-09-08 09:59:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814493, 390359, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is really nice.  i love the point of view, the lowness of the camera.  the angle works terrifically.  it has such an intimate, peaceful and gentle feeling.  the lighting (all natural?) is fantastic.  the landscape looks rugged but inviting... the only pastels i really see is the cardigan, and i''m not sure that it actually qualifies as meeting the challenge in the fullest sense.  But it is there so i''ll let it pass. a really lovely dynamic shot.  9.</td>', 'this is really nice.  i love the point of view, the lowness of the camera.  the angle works terrifically.  it has such an intimate, peaceful and gentle feeling.  the lighting (all natural?) is fantastic.  the landscape looks rugged but inviting... the only pastels i really see is the cardigan, and i''m not sure that it actually qualifies as meeting the challenge in the fullest sense.  But it is there so i''ll let it pass. a really lovely dynamic shot.  9.', '2006-09-08 10:04:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814608, 389119, 63398, '<td valign="top">Very nice....I like the glassine effect of the light on the water.</td>', 'Very nice....I like the glassine effect of the light on the water.', '2006-09-08 10:34:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814627, 390203, 50578, '<td valign="top">Nice title.  At first I was wondering  what is with the knife, Then I read the Title and all came together.  Nice idea.</td>', 'Nice title.  At first I was wondering  what is with the knife, Then I read the Title and all came together.  Nice idea.', '2006-09-08 10:44:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814633, 390139, 50578, '<td valign="top">I think I have seen this place before either in person or in another photo.</td>', 'I think I have seen this place before either in person or in another photo.', '2006-09-08 10:47:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2814948, 389919, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is immensly likeable in most respects, but does suffer a wee bit due to a bit of over processing (either too much noise reduction, or too much over sharpehing, or probably both).  it has the unfortunate effect that the girl looks like a very flat cardboard cut out stuck in front of whatever the background is.  compositionwise it''s great; the negative space is really effective and visually pleasing and intriguing.  the posture, expression and character of the girl is really cool and has a sense of candid realness which feels natural.  the background is really funky and fun, complements the girls jacket and hair really well.  as a whole, this image works asthetically well, and has a great sense of scale.  i''d say it half meets the challenge; the jacket seems merely incidentally pastel, and the background is too mustard to really count. overall, i give it 7.</td>', 'this is immensly likeable in most respects, but does suffer a wee bit due to a bit of over processing (either too much noise reduction, or too much over sharpehing, or probably both).  it has the unfortunate effect that the girl looks like a very flat cardboard cut out stuck in front of whatever the background is.  compositionwise it''s great; the negative space is really effective and visually pleasing and intriguing.  the posture, expression and character of the girl is really cool and has a sense of candid realness which feels natural.  the background is really funky and fun, complements the girls jacket and hair really well.  as a whole, this image works asthetically well, and has a great sense of scale.  i''d say it half meets the challenge; the jacket seems merely incidentally pastel, and the background is too mustard to really count. overall, i give it 7.', '2006-09-08 12:03:40.000000', NULL, 1),
